{{Quote|Since these ones arrived, this territory has been an endless stream of mercenaries seeking reward and bringing destruction.''"<br />"''Then why did you guide me?''"<br />"''They do not belong here. Those that live here come to seek peace. There will be no peace until they're gone.|Kuiil and Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 1" />}}
'''Arvala-7''' was a remote desert [[planet]] with a barren, rocky surface and breathable [[atmosphere]] in the [[Arvala system]] in the [[Sevetta sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. During the [[New Republic Era]], it was home to the [[Ugnaught]] [[Kuiil]], who lived on a [[Kuiil's moisture farm|moisture farm]] with his [[blurrg]]. Sometime after Kuiil moved to the world, a group of [[Nikto]] [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] built an [[Nikto hideout|encampment]], inside which they kept captive a [[youngling]] of the same [[Yoda's species|species]] as the [[Death|late]] [[Jedi Master]] [[Yoda]].

Having accepted a [[Mission to Arvala-7|contract]] to [[Hunt for Grogu|retrieve]] [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] for his [[The Client|client]], the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] traveled to Arvala-7 in his [[gunship]], the ''[[Razor Crest]]''. He met Kuiil after the Ugnaught saved him from a blurrg attack, and the [[farmer]] offered to help Djarin locate his quarry. Kuiil led Djarin to the mercenary encampment on blurrg mounts and left the Mandalorian to capture the asset on his own. With the help of [[IG-11]], an [[IG-series assassin droid]] also working for the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]], Djarin eliminated the Nikto and located Grogu. He then rescued the youngling from IG-11, who intended to kill him per the Client's request.

Upon returning to the ''Razor Crest'', Djarin discovered his ship had been scrapped by local [[Jawa]]s for spare parts. With the help of Kuiil, the bounty hunter negotiated a trade for the parts in exchange for a [[mudhorn egg]]. Djarin traveled into the [[Mudhorn cave|cave]] where the [[mudhorn]] dwelt, and only defeated the beast after Grogu used [[the Force]] to [[Telekinesis|levitate]] it. With the [[egg]] handed over to the Jawas, Djarin was able to repair his [[Starship|ship]] and leave Arvala-7.

Djarin later returned to the planet with [[Carasynthia Dune]] to recruit Kuiil's help in caring for Grogu while they went on a [[Clash on Nevarro|mission]] to the planet [[Nevarro]]. Kuiil agreed to come along only if IG-11, whom the Ugnaught had repaired and [[Programmer|reprogrammed]], and the blurrg were allowed to join. After Djarin reluctantly agreed, the newly formed team departed for Nevarro.

==Description==
{{Quote|No, you will need one. To ride. The way is impossible to pass without a blurrg mount.|Kuiil explains the difficult terrain on Arvala-7|<ref name="Chapter 1" />}}
[[File:Arvala-7_surface.png|thumb|left|275px|The barren, rocky surface of Arvala-7]]
Arvala-7 was an out-of-the-way<ref name="Mando Search">''[[The Mandalorian: A Search-and-Find Book]]''</ref> terrestrial [[planet]] with a barren,<ref name="Chapter 2" /> desert surface<ref name="Mando Search" /> covered in rocky mountains,<ref name="Chapter 2" /> cracked hardened mud, viscous mud flats,<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|arvala-7|Arvala-7}}</ref> canyons, and caves that was incredibly difficult to traverse on foot. The world was [[Homeworld|home]] to several creatures, including [[blurrg]]s, [[mudhorn]]s, [[gorvin snu]], and [[Arges frog|Sorgan frogs]]. Arvala-7 had a breathable [[atmosphere]] that was capable of producing thunderstorms.<ref name="Chapter 2" /> The planet was sparsely populated but shared its name<ref name="Databank" /> with [[Arvala-6|Arvala-Six]], a location that was occupied by the [[Galactic Empire]] during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Aldhani">{{Andor|Aldhani (episode)}}</ref>

==History==
===Hunt for Grogu===
{{Quote|I will help you. I have spoken.|Kuiil offers assistance to Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 1" />}}
[[File:Kuiil_trains_Djarin.png|thumb|right|275px|Kuiil trains Djarin on blurrg-riding.]]
During the [[New Republic Era]], a [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] named [[Din Djarin]] traveled to Arvala-7 after accepting a [[Mission to Arvala-7|contract]] to [[Hunt for Grogu|retrieve]] an [[Din Grogu|asset]] for his [[The Client|client]]. After landing his<ref name="Chapter 1" /> [[gunship]],<ref name="Panel">{{SWYouTube|GrlTosbjylA|The Mandalorian Panel – Sunday|nolive=1}}</ref> called the ''[[Razor Crest]]'', he spotted a herd of blurrgs, two of which quickly attacked him. The [[Ugnaught]] [[Kuiil]] arrived on a blurrg mount and rescued Djarin, taking him to [[Kuiil's moisture farm|his]] [[moisture farm]], where he offered to assist the Mandalorian in locating his [[bounty]]. Kuiil trained Djarin on blurrg riding in preparation for their journey to a nearby [[Nikto hideout|encampment]], and the duo later departed across the rocky terrain.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

After leading Djarin to the encampment, Kuiil departed back to his [[farm]]. While observing the [[Nikto]] [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] in the camp, Djarin noticed an [[IG-series assassin droid]] entering the base and demanding the asset be released, citing the [[Bondsman Guild Protocol]]. The [[assassin droid]], designated [[IG-11]], was immediately attacked, though he [[Death|killed]] many of the mercenaries, sending the rest into hiding within the camp's buildings. Djarin approached IG-11, and the droid initially perceived him as a threat. After revealing himself as a fellow member of the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]], the two negotiated a deal to work together and split the bounty reward.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

[[File:The_Mandalorian_and_the_Asset.png|thumb|left|250px|Djarin saves Grogu.]]
As the remaining Nikto began a second attack, the two worked their way to the back of the camp, where Djarin's [[tracking fob]] indicated the asset was being held. After eliminating the remaining mercenaries, the two used a mounted [[turret]] to blast open the door to the room containing their target. Once inside, they discovered a [[Youngling|child]] of the same species as [[Jedi Master]] [[Yoda]]. When IG-11 aimed his [[E-11 medium blaster rifle]] at the asset, Djarin shot the droid, destroying him.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

===Getting offworld===
{{Quote|You need to drop your rifle.''"<br />"''I'm a Mandalorian. Weapons are part of my religion.|Kuiil gives Djarin advice on trading with Jawas|audio=Djarin-Religion-TMS1C2.flac|<ref name="Chapter 2" />}}
[[File:Arvala-7-Sandcrawler-TheMandalorian.png|thumb|right|275px|Jawas stripped the ''Razor Crest'' for spare parts.]]
With the asset in possession, Djarin made his way back to the ''Razor Crest''. Along the way, he was ambushed by a group of [[Trandoshan]] mercenaries who had been hired by the Guild, though he managed to kill them all. Upon arriving at his gunship, the Mandalorian discovered a group of [[Jawa]]s had gutted the ''Razor Crest'' for spare parts. After an initial failed attempt to pursue the Jawas' [[sandcrawler]], Djarin returned to the remains of his [[Starship|ship]] and then to Kuiil's farm.<ref name="Chapter 2" />

[[File:Mudhorn-TMtAoDD.png|thumb|left|250px|Djarin had to battle a mudhorn to retrieve its egg.]]
Kuiil offered to help Djarin get his ship parts back by taking him to the Jawas so he could negotiate a trade. When they eventually caught up to the Jawas, Djarin, though at first demanding his parts free of charge, agreed to retrieve a [[mudhorn egg]] in exchange for his stolen property. The Jawas drove the bounty hunter to a nearby [[mudhorn cave]] where he confronted the beast. Despite being heavily beaten by the creature, Djarin defeated the mudhorn after the asset used [[the Force]] to [[Telekinesis|levitate]] it, allowing Djarin to stab its head. He then retrieved an [[egg]] and delivered it back to the Jawas, who busted it open and began consuming it.<ref name="Chapter 2" />

With the parts returned to him, Djarin, Kuiil, and the asset returned to the ''Razor Crest''. Kuiil assisted in the repairs, and Djarin offered him a job as a crewmate. The Ugnaught politely declined and thanked the bounty hunter for bringing peace to his valley, and Djarin and the Child left Arvala-7 for [[Nevarro]].<ref name="Chapter 2" />

===Protecting Grogu===
{{Quote|We need someone to watch that thing.|Dune suggests finding someone to care for The Child|<ref name="Chapter 7">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 7: The Reckoning}}</ref>}}
[[File:Djarin_recruits_Kuiil.png|thumb|right|275px|Djarin recruits Kuiil.]]
After receiving a [[hologram]] message from [[Greef Karga]], the head of the Bounty Hunters' Guild, requesting Djarin bring Grogu back to Nevarro to be used as live bait to lure the Client out, as he had made himself an enemy of both Karga and the Guild. Djarin recruited ex-[[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] [[shock trooper]] [[Carasynthia Dune]] on [[Sorgan]], and after leaving the planet, the two brought Grogu back to Arvala-7 to request the assistance of Kuiil in caring for him. Kuiil agreed to join them on their [[Clash on Nevarro|mission]] to Nevarro on the condition that IG-11, whom Kuiil had repaired and [[Programmer|reprogrammed]], and his blurrgs be allowed to come along. After agreeing to the deal, the newly formed team left Arvala-7.<ref name="Chapter 7" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Considering that the work was turned over to us quite late in the schedule, we had to think fast. The final results are a testament to what the team can do with little time and a lot of ingenuity.|Edmond Engelbrecht, CG Supervisor|<ref name="IE.com">{{WebCite|url=https://image-engine.com/case-studies/the-mandalorian-season-1|text=The Mandalorian: Season 1|work=[https://image-engine.com Image-Engine.com]|archivedate=20200810215302}}</ref>}}
[[File:Arvala-7-production.png|thumb|left|275px|Image Engine worked with Industrial Light & Magic on the Arvala-7 scenes.]]
Arvala-7 first appeared in the first episode of the television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Chapter 1" /> which was titled "[[Chapter 1: The Mandalorian]]" and aired on [[November 12]], [[2019]].<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|date=2019-09-24|format=[[Wikipedia:PDF|PDF]]|work=[[Wikipedia:Walt Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International|Walt Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]]|pages=[https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf#page=1]|archivedate=20210623202717}}</ref>

When [[Lucasfilm]] art department designed Arvala-7, the artists tried to find a different take for the then new planet. They thought about taking dried mud and scaling it up so features that were normally a couple of meters across became hundreds of meters. The original brief was that it rained very rarely, every five or seven years, and the events of the ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'' take place between rainy seasons. When [[Rick Famuyiwa]] joined to direct "[[Chapter 2: The Child]]," he wanted to make the planet wetter and give it a little more texture.<ref name="art of">[[The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian (Season One)|''The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season One]]</ref>

[[Image Engine]] was responsible for developing several establishing shots that documented Djarin and Kuiil's journey through the rain to the Jawa camp, as well as working on a sandcrawler render from [[Industrial Light & Magic]] and the bargaining scenes at the camp. Backdrops on Arvala-7 were created using 360-degree LED display monitors, which allowed for interactive backdrop assets to be rendered and displayed in real time. When the light from the LEDs was not enough to simulate real daylight, the team performed heavy grading on props to make them blend with the backdrop. Whenever the real-time background looked out of place, the LED volume was replaced entirely with a computer-generated backdrop. To accomplish this, Image Engine ingested the real-time assets from ILM, uprezzed them in lookdev and texture, made sure cameras lined up properly, and then handed the asset over to the environments department.<ref name="IE.com" />

